# The starter's own repository: nothing personal, nothing machine-specific, nothing generated by local test runs.

# Hook state from working on the starter (usage stats, turn records, diagnostics)
tools/hooks/state/
# Scratch: screenshots, reviews, drafts, git backup bundles
.cache/
# The local blocklist of private terms the publish-safety sweep checks (the list itself is private)
.private-terms
# Marks a development copy of the starter: real projects refuse to be made from it or linked to it
.starter-dev
# Lessons linked projects send back (node tools/starter.mjs report): they name the user's projects and quote their
# words, so they stay on this machine and never reach the public repository
docs/feedback-inbox/
# Agent-specific files, made on each machine by node tools/hooks/wire.mjs (the rules live in AGENTS.md)
CLAUDE.md
.claude/
.codex/
.gemini/
.agents/
tools/starter.local.json
.starter/

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
keys.json

# Backups, logs, dependencies, build and test output
*.bundle
*.orig
*.tmp
logs/
*.log
node_modules/
dist/
build/
coverage/
test-results/
playwright-report/
__pycache__/
.venv/
venv/

# OS and editor clutter (each person's own editor and vault settings)
.obsidian/
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
~$*
*.swp
